        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_50fc2b49ffd241cb92c76d660c6944f6",
      "statement": "The entry point dispatches `check` and `store` on the first argument, importing `paraphe.check` and `paraphe.store_cli` in their own branches before the `--config` loop, so neither owner-side command consumes a `--config` pair and neither starts the server.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/paraphe/__main__.py#L57-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e77518891b51d6ab7637fe8590da81302402dfd56a2f6020427d3893122702ab:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c92c75987e6341ff8ce98b20356bc70d",
      "statement": "`paraphe check telegram` resolves the configuration file itself from `PARAPHE_CONFIG_PATH`, else `paraphe.toml` in the working directory, and feeds it to the same `load_settings` the server uses, so every `SetupError` the loader raises — a missing `mcp_create_bearer`, an invalid owner id or TTL, or the store-location guard — refuses the check with one `paraphe: <message>` line and exit 2 before any Telegram call is made.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/paraphe/check.py#L28-L42",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:42d37b28621168526937a889b97cbac4fb70cc718d4e357837b4d5bbeaad8f90:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/paraphe/inbox/config.py#L110-L182",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ea55dc481398e303606d46503512ccc6fed5f1260313660ebae37565d888cd00:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9d29f988c5b24215a818e3723dc75106",
      "statement": "The check refuses with `paraphe: no phone destination is configured` and exit 2 in two distinguishable situations: a configuration file that does not exist together with no non-blank `PARAPHE_BOT_TOKEN` or `PARAPHE_OWNER_TELEGRAM_ID`, decided before settings are loaded, and resolved settings that carry no bot token, decided after; in the first case the Bot API client is never constructed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/paraphe/check.py#L28-L42",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:42d37b28621168526937a889b97cbac4fb70cc718d4e357837b4d5bbeaad8f90:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/inbox/test_check.py#L131-L142",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:62dc478d1eeb11dbc61826fa51d5084d4529c4babcf8085173842723b7680335:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8b9c8255139e40cd80e7a0ea56f8ee11",
      "statement": "After settings resolve, the check calls `getMe` and prints the bot identity as `@<username>` when the identity carries a username, else `the configured bot`, then sends the fixed plain `CHECK_MESSAGE` to the configured owner id with `reply_markup` of `None` and no parse mode, and prints `Telegram check passed for owner <id>.` with exit 0 only when both calls succeed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/paraphe/check.py#L14-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4a0bebd986203683f9e0fd59e00ad83943034fb88cf6d219d4440b3802ec6e6b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/paraphe/check.py#L44-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:10f0ca4456b842911fa2804910e4e5775321231e6bc9bb48ccdb6bf2da295c1c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/inbox/test_check.py#L57-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b69f6dc1952d75fcbad8fa5958daf36b53b36b163eaa6083788e7f92818028da:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5eca9f4ac87d4c29b4415cd440a6b971",
      "statement": "The check maps a request Telegram refused (`NotifyRejected`) and a request it could not reach (`TelegramAPIError`) to different messages for both `getMe` and delivery — `Telegram refused the configured bot token` or `Telegram could not deliver to owner <id>; check the id and open a private chat with the bot first` versus `could not reach the Telegram Bot API` — all with exit 2, so a transport failure is never reported as a Telegram refusal and a network failure never blames the owner id.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/paraphe/check.py#L44-L67",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:50514e8dd8b5ea521bf45cef36798f14b357e693fc0c5043c6dca1da2fe3e0d3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/paraphe/inbox/runtime.py#L85-L111",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9e532dfdc90fa7dc6dcaf02198b0b590aa784e2a0167b31d3b948569ef7df5ac:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/inbox/test_check.py#L83-L129",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e88035e769eba98a8f5f95d27c75f3f66a1c98802981bcf536d1314b116e7f13:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3b73ca67a0ab4d1c93bbfaaeada9d4a4",
      "statement": "The check creates no decision card: it never opens the store, records no notification and no Telegram message id, sends one plain message with no buttons, and prints neither the bot token nor the token-bearing request URL — the suite asserts both absences on the pass path and on each refusal path.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/paraphe/check.py#L44-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:10f0ca4456b842911fa2804910e4e5775321231e6bc9bb48ccdb6bf2da295c1c:"
