    {
      "id": "claim_4e23c8f20933416396dedc3a5d29a881",
      "statement": "`paraphe store relocate` computes its own endpoints — `LEGACY_STORE_PATH` (`/var/lib/paraphe/inbox.sqlite`) as the source and `default_store_path()` as the target — and takes no location arguments and no configuration, so it is the upgrade from the retained legacy location rather than a general-purpose move to an arbitrary path.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/paraphe/inbox/store.py#L12-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c3bc6ac4744b24f208c254d5f2f4f3a9517a4bd02b059d87dae1e3c47d0c37e1:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/paraphe/store_cli.py#L26-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:17afab2f72de65623f55d1049356992adc1ffd61e5a9fba2071f637a4c387bfe:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_34e05a0418b74b24bf75f25258ba5db6",
      "statement": "`relocate_store` refuses before changing the filesystem when the source is missing (`source store does not exist: <source>`), the target is occupied (`target store already exists: <target>`), both names resolve to one location (`source and target store are the same`), or either path cannot be read, which is reported as one line naming that path, and a refused run leaves the source and any existing target bytes untouched.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/paraphe/inbox/store.py#L58-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1925941ce52e76d9f55b535ac9ad0ce5d3ec52eeaaf58a3fc6e6ea1ddce26e18:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/inbox/test_setup.py#L305-L317",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:74c4c7b7dafd3fe294e37a135c0eb07b4a2fd5566a1179f4724a5549bd5264c2:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/inbox/test_setup.py#L332-L347",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7f4f9663c33b93272eb56cc2c367ad7ad7f2ce6ae758afec89f7680e0e5c03c3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fbf59226155b4db1b8f98562f14dbefb",
      "statement": "Relocation creates the destination directory with `mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)` plus an explicit `chmod` to 0700 (failure: `data directory is not usable: <dir>`), builds the copy under a temporary `.tmp` name in that same directory while deliberately not creating the final database path, and takes the snapshot with SQLite's `backup` API from a read-only (`mode=ro`) source connection instead of copying live database bytes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/paraphe/inbox/store.py#L77-L111",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b2396586a7883babe27ae53cf054b1a67e2c9766bfe9ffb0b90ddd37a4fc128e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5e6179a9c9444200b5f8fa799cf0b2c9",
      "statement": "The snapshot must pass `PRAGMA integrity_check` with `ok` and must contain the `cards` table before it is installed, because the integrity check alone also passes an empty or foreign database; failures are `copied store failed its integrity check` or `source store is not a Paraphe store: <source>` and leave no target file or leftover temporary file.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/paraphe/inbox/store.py#L113-L131",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1a44492adcf494631fcb577c8bc57fabf85ca4db96176afbf97ba9f1c6ff8078:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/inbox/test_setup.py#L319-L361",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dc09d3ff3f021b0a79a94d945527a2f1bcf8ce3a213192dc8ea5b19cee04c07b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6d76f5649fee42929f6e780224b20eb4",
      "statement": "Installation sets the copy to 0600 and links it to the target with `os.link`, which refuses rather than overwrites a target that appeared meanwhile (reported as `target store already exists: <target>`), then chmods the target to 0600 and removes the temporary name; an `OSError` after the link removes the target again, so a completed relocation is a 0600 file inside a 0700 directory.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/paraphe/inbox/store.py#L133-L151",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:32de53f0ef9e6b59a999a11df2410f30e4d5c28a464f5cb7d7821a9b38893345:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/inbox/test_setup.py#L265-L291",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e178d7e38a4b355e8d6e0bd1c13241df07d5da610d7f0abb48ff6a82aa8a8b3c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5385f7591e63498db8071751cca4c95d",
      "statement": "With `--move`, the source is removed only after the verified target exists; if that removal fails the target is removed as a rollback and the command refuses with `could not remove source store: <source>`, so a move that cannot complete leaves the store only where it started.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/paraphe/inbox/store.py#L153-L163",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c31b89c05be201e1050843ef0a1582682042dae58a9dae57aab3f2dc236824b3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/inbox/test_setup.py#L293-L303",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:07716b2385b85fdd783f1994af4358e8bd28fc4ecdcf39595fe2bba7106346a0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2c0eb7c0d8cf44d7a68cdefd34608c63",
      "statement": "Every failure path removes the unfinished snapshot in a `finally`; a `sqlite3.Error` becomes `store could not be copied: <source>` and any other `OSError` becomes `store could not be relocated: <source>`, which `store_cli` prints as one `paraphe: <message>` line on stderr with exit 2, while success prints `Copied store from <source> to <target>.` or `Moved store from <source> to <target>.` on stdout and exits 0.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/paraphe/inbox/store.py#L164-L176",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d6e19ce56ce9a6b60dfa18ad8b06cb98c5c96080a6b1eb27f1a263e577db2a45:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/paraphe/store_cli.py#L29-L37",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:07cc03313d1ac5be28e112e428e0c42cb9ba3ea3f34af687e98792fd40208903:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_47d64b686cde4872ac4d5564b82bbb92",
      "statement": "Relocation does not replace the startup guard: `resolve_store_path` still refuses when an unconfigured default holds no store while the retained legacy location holds one, an explicit `store_path` is still honoured even then, and once the verified copy lands at the default the guard's condition can no longer be met so startup proceeds against the relocated store.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/paraphe/inbox/config.py#L110-L127",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2de812415bd677379a04012596d9df37d388be45826c537d212e53d0ba52e44f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/inbox/test_setup.py#L242-L263",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0f9606c63ed8d292e02c6fae8d2c0c30f0ca3e129cc70f8c68e10fa23b7fa677:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/inbox/test_setup.py#L424-L436",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f5155eabbc8d8c6c22533924c6345073661b43f1f8ce10cd9ff7b8677e192b40:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ed1838fb661345e886a848f61d5d3208",
      "statement": "`tests/inbox/test_check.py` witnesses the preflight (exit 0 only after identity and delivery, the two refusal classes, the no-configuration case with the API never constructed, leak-free output, and routing through `paraphe.__main__.main`) and `tests/inbox/test_setup.py` witnesses relocation end to end (data preserved with owner-only modes, move only with the flag, refused and failed copies leaving neither target nor temporary file, and startup accepting the relocated default).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/inbox/test_check.py#L35-L161",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:89530e7d2ae1823daad881f3e15d2cca54810fbbaaae1014aff603242cb6f278:"
        },
